  "reason": "No experiments have been completed, so the critical first question is: what is the performance floor of the simplest possible model? config_001 (RNA-only, single profile, PCA n2000) is the most minimal configuration in the search space—it uses a linear projection, a single profile (no aggregation), and no image or fusion components. Running this first establishes the baseline RNA signal strength with minimal assumptions, which is essential for interpreting all subsequent experiments. If this baseline is already competitive, it tells us that complex encoders (scVI, scGPT) or multimodal fusion may offer diminishing returns; if it is weak, it motivates exploring richer RNA encoders or adding the image modality. Choosing the simplest configuration first also minimizes computational cost, preserving budget for the many follow-up comparisons (encoder choice, profile setting, aggregation, fusion) that will follow. This single experiment reduces the most uncertainty with the least risk of confounding, since no design choice is 'turned on' simultaneously."
}

